    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2WCDZsDJ9sgBpcwvxPEonRo)_\n\n## Why\nOn macOS the frame made by `sp-quick-capture-popup` (#131) was blank and Emacs hung (beachball), and AeroSpace tiled it to full size. `org-protocol` would not help: it opens the same frame.\n\n## What\n- `tools/quick-capture-native`: `osascript` shows a native dialog for the line, the script sends it to the running Emacs with `emacsclient -e '(sp-quick-capture \"…\")'` (backslashes and quotes escaped), and a notification shows what was written or the error. No Emacs frame, so nothing for AeroSpace to tile or for `mini-frame` to interfere with.\n- `sp-quick-capture` now returns the preview text (used for the notification). New ERT test; 9 tests pass in Emacs 29.3 batch.\n- Doc and CHANGELOG updated. The Emacs-frame path is left in place but marked unconfirmed.\n\n## Not tested\nThe script itself (dialog, focus, notification) was not run: no macOS here. Only the escaping and the Elisp side were checked.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nv18Dts2Bw3SSBDEV1kzyy)_",
